WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.657
The future rarely unfolds exactly as expected.

00:00:02.657 --> 00:00:07.040
Structured techniques encourage analysts to explore alternative futures and identify factors that

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.866
could lead to different outcomes.

00:00:08.866 --> 00:00:11.423
This work often begins with key assumptions.

00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:15.075
If a major assumption changes, what paths become more likely?

00:00:15.075 --> 00:00:19.458
What early indicators would suggest movement toward one path instead of another?

00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:22.380
Considering multiple possibilities improves preparedness and reduces overconfidence.

00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:28.224
It helps teams plan for uncertainty instead of treating one forecast as the only plausible outcome.

00:00:28.224 --> 00:00:30.416
The objective is not precise prediction.

00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:34.434
The objective is understanding what could happen, why it could happen,

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.260
and how organizations might respond.
